                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Stay far away\n\nI really wanted to like this game, but after a few weeks I can honestly say it's one of the most player-unfriendly experiences I've ever had. Save your money and your sanity.\n\nPay-to-win in the worst way. If you don't open your wallet, you simply don't get to play. Free players are treated like second-class citizens, locked out of the content that actually matters. The game isn't \"free-to-play,\" it's \"pay-to-play-with-extra-steps.\"\n\nA mindless grind that feels like a second job. There's no fun to be had here — just endless repetition. You have to grind like you're clocking in for a shift, and even then you barely progress. It's not engaging, it's exhausting.\n\nOnly paid loadouts matter. The only people actually competing are the ones running premium gear. Everyone else is just cannon fodder. Skill means nothing when someone can buy their way to the top.\n\nAnd here's the real scam: when you buy premium weapons, they only let you enjoy them for about three months. After that, they nerf them into the ground and immediately sell you the next shiny paid weapon. It's a never-ending cycle designed to squeeze you dry. You're not buying a weapon — you're renting it until they decide it's time to sell you a new one.\n\nThe servers are a joke. They lag so badly that I'm lucky to get into a match on the fifth try. Half the time I can't even connect, and when I do, the lag makes it unplayable.\n\nFinal verdict: This game is a cash grab built on frustration. It disrespects your time, your wallet, and your intelligence. Do yourself a favor and play literally anything else.",
